ng{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-19T14:21:33Z","updated_at":"2025-04-19T14:21:33Z","body":"> Adding points to the curve won't trigger the setter function\n\nThis is correct/intended behavior. Adding points to curve is not re-setting/re-assigning the property (curve), hence no setter is called. To detect changes to the Curve assigned to the property you can connect to its `Resource.changed` signal:\n\n```gdscript\n@tool\nextends Node2D\n\n@export var test : Curve:\n\tset(value):\n\t\tprint(\"Setter was called\")\n\t\tif test == value:\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\tif is_instance_valid(test):\n\t\t\ttest.changed.disconnect(_on_test_curve_changed)\n\t\ttest = value\n\t\tif is_instance_valid(test):\n\t\t\ttest.changed.connect(_on_test_curve_changed)\n\nfunc _on_test_curve_changed() -> void:\n\tprint(\"test.changed\")\n```\n\nClosing as not a bug.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816726569/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]